      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 30-year-old woman developed ischemia-like chest pain due to myocardial compression by an intracardiac cyst. The cyst was located in the interventricular septum. Its etiology could not be ascertained despite several diagnostic measures but exstirpation was indicated by the clinical symptoms. Intraoperatively the diagnosis of echinococcosis was established. The cyst was extirpated in toto without perforation of the thinned interventricular septum. Postoperatively the patient was symptomfree."},
